#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Island, from its boot out of its Information Center and onto the
# island, and away on a bike (#124).
#
# Recorded, not written: a synthetic hand in lego_island.rs (`ride`) did this
# through the host, as a person's hand reaches a run in a window, and the run
# wrote down what it was handed. The pointer glides a few pixels a flip; a
# button is held two flips; a key as long as it is held.
#
# Until flip 5149 nothing is pressed, which is information-center.route. Then,
# in the Information Center: the blue brick on the desk opens the registration
# book, L, E, G and O are typed on the keyboard, and the tick signs the book.
# Then Pepper's portrait: his movie plays and he is who the player is. The
# island lets nobody out who has not signed and picked someone, and a new name
# picks nobody, so the book comes first. The arrow at the left goes to the
# elevator, the arrow at its left to the revolving door, and the door out:
# from flip 12100 the island is seen through the doorway. Outside, Up walks a
# step forward and Left turns to face the red bicycle by the door. It is
# clicked at flip 13317, its handlebars are in front of the camera by
# flip 13400, and Up rides it away down the road from flip 13600 to 13800.
